      "classification": "valid_baseline",
      "reason": "For every allowed nonzero coefficient vector, choose two active coefficients. Their exponent difference is coprime to N; the nondegenerate real-line/circle intersection bounds its power image by two. One active coefficient is handled separately, and an inactive third coefficient causes no degeneracy in the line argument."
    },
    {
      "id": "arbitrary-modulus-triple",
      "response_lines": [
        22,
        40
      ],
      "classification": "valid_R3_structure",
      "reason": "The map z↦(z^d,z^e) has kernel μ_g. For three active coefficients, each of at most two first-coordinate values fixes the second, hence the full zero set is a union of at most two g-point fibers. Interpolating at 1 and a primitive n-th root gives a rank-two matrix with every two-column minor nonzero; this proves all coefficients are active and the two fibers distinct. The binary cases attain the separate gcd bounds. Thus the stated exact maximum is proved on every modulus and fixed triple, already a sufficient 1.1 R3 anchor."
    },
    {
      "id": "prime-power-all-support-classification",
      "response_lines": [
        44,
        105
      ],
      "classification": "valid_R3_structure",
      "reason": "Checked both directions for arbitrary nonempty A and all m≤N, including m=1,N and q=0/s=0. Sufficiency correctly compares the p-adic valuations of all pairwise differences to those of 0,…,m−1. The integer alternant quotient survives ζ↦1 mod p because its all-one value is a p-unit. Necessity uses q complete μ_d cosets plus s points: a residue count below q forces total rank<qd+s, while a count above ceil(m/d) supplies a nonzero class-supported kernel. Every imbalance falls into one of these two branches."
    },
    {
      "id": "interpolation-and-exact-zero-sets",
      "response_lines": [
        107,
        117
      ],
      "classification": "valid_additional_theorem",
      "reason": "The replaced-column determinant is the Lagrange cardinal polynomial in V_A. Every ≤m-node evaluation has maximal rank by extension to m nodes. For |T|<m, each undesired additional zero cuts K_T by a proper hyperplane; a finite union cannot exhaust a complex vector space. This proves exact realization, and the m−1 case has a one-dimensional coefficient space. No unproved full-support claim is added."
    },
